# {{projectName}}

Built with pasha CLI — **Event-Driven / Event Sourcing** on NestJS.

## Core principles

- **Domain events are the source of truth** — every state change is recorded as an immutable event
- **CQRS read/write split** — commands produce events, queries read from projections
- **Event Store** — append-only log, stores all events keyed by aggregate ID
- **Aggregates** — rebuild state by replaying events, emit uncommitted events on mutation
- **Projections** — build denormalized read models from events (in-memory, swappable to Redis/DB)
- **Outbox pattern** — events are written to store + outbox in same transaction (where DB-backed), then published to the message broker asynchronously

## Module structure

```
src/features/<module>/
├── commands/         ← command + handler (validate → load aggregate → mutate → append events)
├── events/           ← domain event classes (data classes)
├── aggregates/       ← event-sourced aggregate (rebuilds from event stream)
├── projections/      ← builds read model from events
├── event-store/      ← append/get events (immutable log)
├── dto/              ← HTTP request shapes
└── infrastructure/
    ├── <module>.controller.ts
    ├── <module>.module.ts
    └── outbox/       ← publishes events to broker
```
